<title>UK: Prudential says agrees deal on pension sales.</title>
<headline>Prudential says agrees deal on pension sales.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's largest insurance group, Prudential Corp, said on Tuesday it had agreed to compensate some of the victims of personal pensions mis-selling.</p>
<p>Prudential has reached an agreement with Britain's GMB general union in return for an end to litigation in the courts.</p>
<p>But the company declined to comment on press reports that the cost of the deal was around 800,000 pounds.</p>
<p>The union had instigated legal action against a number of companies over the mis-selling of personal pensions.</p>
<p>Under Monday's deal, Prudential will pay redress in 13 cases where writs have been issued and agree &quot;a timely resolution&quot; of the remaining 30 cases involving GMB members.</p>
<p>-- Simon Cowell, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7721</p>
</text>
